 "summary": {
  "version": 2,
  "basis": "em",
  "attribution": "Written by a model from the explanatory memorandum; not the record",
  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2018-02-15",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would extend waiting periods for newly arrived residents to receive specified social security payments and concession cards, generally from 104 weeks to 156 weeks.",
   "It would also introduce 156-week waiting periods for family tax benefit, parental leave pay and dad and partner pay, expanding the payments subject to waiting.",
   "Existing social security exemptions for refugees and citizens would remain, with earlier visa holders generally covered by the current rules rather than the new periods."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Carer allowance would become subject to a 156-week waiting period, with specified exemptions.",
   "Bereavement allowance, widow allowance and parenting payment would receive new waiting periods alongside existing qualification requirements.",
   "The farm household allowance waiting period would increase from 104 to 156 weeks.",
   "The special benefit exemption for changed circumstances would require the relevant change to occur after the person's waiting period began."
  ],
  "affected": "Newly arrived residents seeking covered payments or concession cards, including eligible carers, parents and farm household allowance claimants, would be affected.",
